04 — Accessibility
The one place I'd call out as a real gap
I measured this rather than eyeballing it: checked label-to-control association through the DOM, computed real contrast ratios by rasterising each colour through canvas (Tailwind v4 emits oklch(), which naive parsers get wrong), and inspected focus styling.

High
Every form label is unassociated — clicking a label does not focus its field
Contact.jsx:117,131,147,162
All four labels are plain <label> elements with no htmlFor, and the inputs have no id — I confirmed label.control is null for every one. Screen-reader users hear "edit text, blank" instead of "Your Email, edit text". A pointer user who clicks the word "Message" gets nothing. This is the classic WCAG 1.3.1 / 3.3.2 failure and it's four attributes to fix.

<label htmlFor="contact-email" className="...">Your Email</label>
<input
  id="contact-email"
  name="email"
  type="email"
  autoComplete="email"
  required
  aria-required="true"
  value={formData.email}
  onChange={handleChange}
/>
Also add autoComplete="name" / "email" — it lets password managers and phone autofill work, and browsers score it under WCAG 1.3.5.

