06 — Security
Clean on secrets and dependencies — but the contact form is a genuine problem
Dependency audit: 0 vulnerabilities. npm audit reports found 0 vulnerabilities, and a manual grep for API keys, tokens, secrets, passwords and sk-…-shaped strings across all source and config files returns nothing. There is no .env, and no client-side secret pattern to leak. Every target="_blank" link correctly pairs with rel="noreferrer" (which also implies noopener), closing the reverse-tabnabbing hole that's usually the one real issue on portfolio sites. There is no dangerouslySetInnerHTML anywhere, so React's escaping covers the input surface.
High
The contact form reports success without sending anything
Contact.jsx:22–26
handleSubmit calls preventDefault() and then setSubmitted(true). Nothing else. I instrumented window.fetch and XMLHttpRequest, filled the form and submitted it: zero network requests were made, and the UI showed "Message Received! … I will review your message and get back to you shortly."

This is the highest-impact issue in the repo, and it isn't a security hole — it's a trust hole. Any recruiter or collaborator who uses that form believes they reached you and will never follow up by email, because the page told them it worked. On a portfolio, the contact form is the conversion path.

// Honest minimal fix — works with no backend at all
const handleSubmit = (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const subject = encodeURIComponent(formData.subject);
  const body = encodeURIComponent(
    `${formData.message}\n\n— ${formData.name} (${formData.email})`
  );
  window.location.href = `mailto:pradhanshreejal0@gmail.com?subject=${subject}&body=${body}`;
  setSubmitted(true);
};
Better options, in order of quality: (1) a real endpoint — Formspree, Web3Forms, Netlify Forms or a small /api/contact on Vercel; (2) the mailto: fallback above, with the success copy changed to "Your email app should now be open"; (3) if you genuinely don't want messages, remove the form entirely and keep the email/GitHub cards, which already work. What you must not keep is a form that lies.

