Low
No XSS surface today — but note the one pattern to avoid
Contact.jsx:100
Thank you for reaching out, {formData.name} is rendered as a React text node, so it is escaped and safe. Worth flagging for the future: if a real backend is added and you ever render the echoed value with dangerouslySetInnerHTML (e.g. to support line breaks in a message), that becomes stored XSS. Use white-space: pre-wrap instead of injecting HTML.

07 — SEO & meta tags
The basics are right; everything social is missing
Present and correct: <title> (60 chars, name + role), meta description (155 chars, keyword-rich), charset, viewport, lang="en", a semantic h1 containing the real name.

High
No Open Graph or Twitter Card tags — shared links render as a bare URL
index.html
For a portfolio, the primary distribution channel is being pasted into a chat, a DM or a tweet. With zero og: or twitter: tags, every one of those shares shows a naked link with no title, no description and no image — measurably worse click-through than a rich card. I confirmed the built dist/index.html contains none.

<meta property="og:type"        content="website" />
<meta property="og:title"       content="Shreejal Pradhan — MERN-Stack Developer" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Fullstack developer building scalable web apps with React, Node.js and MongoDB." />
<meta property="og:image"       content="https://your-domain.com/og.png" />
<meta property="og:url"         content="https://your-domain.com/" />

<meta name="twitter:card"        content="summary_large_image" />
<meta name="twitter:title"       content="Shreejal Pradhan — MERN-Stack Developer" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Fullstack developer building scalable web apps." />
<meta name="twitter:image"       content="https://your-domain.com/og.png" />
Use absolute URLs for og:image and og:url — relative paths are ignored by most scrapers. A 1200×630 PNG is the size that renders without cropping.

Medium
The page is 100% client-rendered, so <body> is empty without JS
index.html
The entire HTML payload a crawler receives before executing JavaScript is <div id="root"></div>. Google renders JS and will cope, but Bing and most link-preview bots don't — which compounds the missing-OG problem. Cheapest real fix: put a meaningful <noscript> block and the name/role text in the static HTML.

<div id="root">
  <noscript>
    <h1>Shreejal Pradhan — MERN-Stack Developer</h1>
    <p>Fullstack developer building scalable web apps with MongoDB, Express, React and Node.js.
       Reach me at <a href="mailto:pradhanshreejal0@gmail.com">pradhanshreejal0@gmail.com</a>.</p>
