Medium
The build needs Node ≥ 22.12, but nothing in the repo says so
package.json
On the sandbox's Node 20, npm install printed EBADENGINE for @rolldown/plugin-babel, which declares node >=22.12. The build happened to succeed anyway, but new contributors and most CI images default to Node 18 or 20 and will hit this immediately — with a warning that looks ignorable and isn't guaranteed to be.

// package.json
"engines": { "node": ">=22.12" }

// and add .nvmrc containing: 22
Or remove the cause. @rolldown/plugin-babel exists only to run the React Compiler, which — per the performance section — has nothing to optimise in this codebase. Deleting the Babel plugin, @rolldown/plugin-babel and babel-plugin-react-compiler restores Node 20 compatibility and simplifies the build. Two problems, one deletion.

