11 — Worth considering, not urgent
Two bigger swings, only if you want them
Add a screenshot to each project card
The cards are all text. For a portfolio, a single 16:9 thumbnail per project does more for credibility than any amount of description. Ship them as webp at ~700 px wide, loading="lazy", and give each a real alt — it's the one place where adding images is clearly worth the payload you currently don't have.

Consider Astro or plain HTML later
This page has two pieces of state. Shipping 266 kB of React to render static text is a lot of machinery, and an Astro build would put the same markup on the wire for near-zero JS — which also solves the client-rendered SEO problem outright. Don't rewrite it today: the current app is working, and the fixes above matter far more than the framework choice.

